<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Last_Bastion#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Proxima%20Targeting%20VI">Proxima Targeting VI</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The <i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;&Omega;</i> technology doubles hits before abilities that cancel hits, such as <i>Proxima Targeting VI</i>, are resolved. The planet is still exhausted if the Bastion player controls it.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;X89 turns all hits into 2 before abilities and effects like Titan&rsquo;s agent or Proxima. You will exhaust the planet.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Abilities that affect bombardment rolls, such as the <i>Plasma Scoring</i> technology, the <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player&rsquo;s commander, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Leaders:~:text=Trrakan%20Aun%20Zulok">Trrakan Aun Zulok</a>, or the <a href="/F_jol_nar">Jol&ndash;Nar</a> player&rsquo;s commander, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Leaders:~:text=Agnlan%20Oln">Agnlan Oln</a>, may be applied to the <sc>Bombardment</sc> roll from <i>Proxima Targeting VI</i>.<sup>6,9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Proxima Targeting VI (Technology): Can the Bastion player apply abilities such as Plasma Scoring/Argent commander or Jol-Nar commander to the BOMBARDMENT roll? A: Yes&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>9</sup> Designer Q&amp;A, &ldquo;Unit Abilities imply Units?&rdquo; (on relics and technologies that use unit abilities).</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the Bastion player makes the <sc>Bombardment</sc> roll against their own units, they will be able to cancel a hit for each of their present galvanized units.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Proxima Targeting VI: &ldquo;Cancel 1 hit produced by BOMBARDMENT rolls made against your ground forces for each of your galvanized units present.&rdquo; Its second ability makes &ldquo;an identical roll against your own ground forces,&rdquo; which is a BOMBARDMENT roll against the Bastion player&rsquo;s ground forces.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Other players with galvanized units cannot cancel the <sc>Bombardment</sc> hits produced by <i>Proxima Targeting VI</i>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: The cancel ability is on Proxima Targeting VI (&ldquo;for each of your galvanized units present&rdquo;), which only its owner has. Galvanize gives other players&rsquo; units only this: &ldquo;Galvanized units roll 1 additional die for combat rolls and unit abilities.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Last_Bastion#Space_Dock:~:text=4X41C">4X41C &ldquo;Helios&rdquo;</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The planet&rsquo;s resource value is increased by two with Helios II, not three; the bonuses of Helios I and Helios II do not stack.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do the Last Bastion&rsquo;s spaceport card, Helios upgrade and Galvanize tokens work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Helios II replaces Helios I, so +2, not +3.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <sc>Production</sc> value of the 4X41C &ldquo;Helios&rdquo; will be calculated from the modified resource value of the planet, after the increase from the 4X41C &ldquo;Helios&rdquo; present.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: 4X41C &ldquo;Helios&rdquo;: &ldquo;This unit&rsquo;s PRODUCTION value is equal to 2 more than the resource value of this planet. The resource value of this planet is increased by 1.&rdquo; The planet&rsquo;s resource value is the increased one while the space dock is there, and PRODUCTION reads that value.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Last_Bastion#Flagship:~:text=The%20Egeiro">The Egeiro</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Bastion player controls multiple planets in a system, <i>The Egeiro</i> will apply +1 to its combat rolls just once.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: The Egeiro: &ldquo;Apply +1 to the results of each of this unit&rsquo;s combat rolls for each non-home system that contains a planet you control.&rdquo; The bonus counts systems, not planets.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Bastion player controls a planet in a system, and other players control other planets in that system, <i>The Egeiro</i> will still apply +1 to its combat rolls from that system.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: The Egeiro counts each &ldquo;non-home system that contains a planet you control.&rdquo; A system with one Bastion planet meets that, whoever controls the other planets in it.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Last_Bastion#Leaders:~:text=Dame%20Briar">Dame Briar</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Any type of unit in the same system may be galvanized; it need not match the type of the destroyed unit.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook, Dame Briar (Bastion commander) card text: &ldquo;You may exhaust this card to galvanize another of that player&rsquo;s units in the destroyed unit&rsquo;s system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Last_Bastion#Leaders:~:text=Nip%20and%20Tuck">Nip and Tuck</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Bastion player&rsquo;s action cards may still be canceled by other game effects, such as the <a href="/F_empyrean">Empyrean</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Mech:~:text=Watcher">Watcher</a> mech.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Nip and Tuck: &ldquo;Your action cards cannot be canceled by &lsquo;Sabotage&rsquo; action cards.&rdquo; Only Sabotage is named. The Watcher mech cancels in its own way: &ldquo;remove this unit ... to cancel an action card played by that player.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player already has a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator">Valefar Assimilator</a> token on one of the Bastion player&rsquo;s components, it will remain there when Nip and Tuck are unlocked.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Nip and Tuck: &ldquo;The Nekro Virus cannot place assimilator tokens on your components.&rdquo; It stops new placements; it does not remove a token already placed.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Last_Bastion#Leaders:~:text=Lyra%20Keen">Lyra Keen</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Last_Bastion#Leaders:~:text=Entity%204X41A">Entity 4X41A &ldquo;Apollo&rdquo;</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Any combat roll modifiers will not apply to the dice roll for <i>Entity 4X41A &ldquo;Apollo&rdquo;</i>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Apollo: &ldquo;roll 1 die for each unit in its system that belongs to another player; if the result is equal to or greater than the galvanized unit&rsquo;s combat value, destroy that unit.&rdquo; This is not a combat roll (LRR 18.1: &ldquo;During combat, if a unit&rsquo;s combat roll produces a result ...&rdquo;), so modifiers to combat rolls do not apply.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Units can only be destroyed by the dice specifically allocated to them.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Apollo rolls &ldquo;1 die for each unit&rdquo; and, if &ldquo;the result is equal to or greater than the galvanized unit&rsquo;s combat value, destroy that unit.&rdquo; Each die belongs to one unit and can only destroy that unit.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Effects that cancel hits, such as <sc>Sustain Damage</sc>, cannot be used to prevent units from being destroyed.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Sustain Damage save a ship from &hellip; &lsquo;destroy&rsquo; effects?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; Sustain Damage only cancels hits, and these effects destroy units without producing hits.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>All units belonging to other players in the system may be destroyed, including structures.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Apollo rolls for &ldquo;each unit in its system that belongs to another player.&rdquo; LRR 85: &ldquo;A structure is a type of unit.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If <i>Entity 4X41A &ldquo;Apollo&rdquo;</i> is resolved during combat, units that belong to another player other than the Bastion player&rsquo;s opponent could be destroyed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Apollo rolls for each unit &ldquo;that belongs to another player&rdquo;, not only the opponent&rsquo;s units.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If <i>Entity 4X41A &ldquo;Apollo&rdquo;</i> is resolved during a space combat, ground forces on planets or being transported in that system could be destroyed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Apollo rolls for &ldquo;each unit in its system,&rdquo; not only units in the combat. LRR 88.5: &ldquo;Planets are located in systems.&rdquo; Units on planets or being transported are in the system.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If <i>Entity 4X41A &ldquo;Apollo&rdquo;</i> is resolved during a ground combat, ground forces on other planets or units in the space area of that system could be destroyed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Apollo rolls for &ldquo;each unit in its system,&rdquo; not only units on the planet in combat. LRR 88.5: &ldquo;Planets are located in systems.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>During combat, both players assign hits simultaneously. If the Bastion player wishes to use <i>Entity 4X41A &ldquo;Apollo&rdquo;</i> after destroying one of their units by assigning a hit to it, their opponent would first finish assigning the hits produced by the Bastion player. Only then could the Bastion player resolve <i>Entity 4X41A &ldquo;Apollo&rdquo;</i>, rolling for just their opponent&rsquo;s units that were not destroyed by the assigned hits.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: LRR 78.6: &ldquo;Each player in the combat must choose and destroy one of their own ships in the active system for each hit their opponent produced.&rdquo; Both players assign hits in the same step, so the opponent&rsquo;s assignment finishes as part of the step that destroys the galvanized unit; Apollo then rolls for the units left.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Before assigning hits, players may cancel the produced hits by using the <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability of their units in the combat, one at a time, starting with the active player (intermixed with any other abilities either player wishes to resolve during the same window). Should any of the Bastion player&rsquo;s units be destroyed by a <i>Direct Hit</i> action card, then they can immediately trigger <i>Entity 4X41A &ldquo;Apollo&rdquo;</i>. They will roll dice for all of their opponent&rsquo;s remaining units in the system, which may include some units that their opponent would have otherwise gone on to cancel a hit with by using its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability. Once <i>Entity 4X41A &ldquo;Apollo&rdquo;</i> has finished resolving, both players must assign any remaining hits; they may cancel some number of these by using the <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability of any surviving units in the combat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: LRR 78.6a: &ldquo;Before assigning hits, players may use their units&rsquo; &lsquo;Sustain Damage&rsquo; abilities to cancel hits.&rdquo; LRR 1.19: abilities in the same window are resolved &ldquo;in initiative order, beginning with the active player.&rdquo; Apollo triggers &ldquo;When one of your galvanized units is destroyed,&rdquo; so it resolves in that window, before the remaining hits are assigned.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>During the <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> step of a tactical action, players resolve the <sc>Space Cannon</sc> ability of their eligible units starting with the active player, and going around the table in a clockwise order. Each player will make their space cannon roll and have the hits assigned, likely destroying some units, before the next player begins their own space cannon roll. Should the Bastion player have one of their units destroyed by another player&rsquo;s space cannon roll, and choose to use the ability of <i>Entity 4X41A &ldquo;Apollo&rdquo;</i>, then in doing so they destroy a unit with the <sc>Space Cannon</sc> ability, that unit will not perform a space cannon roll if the player that owns that unit has not yet made their space cannon roll.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When several players fire Space Cannon Offense, are they resolved together?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; one player at a time &hellip; Each player&rsquo;s roll, hit assignment, Sustain Damage and responses like Direct Hit finish before the next fires, so a unit destroyed earlier &hellip; never gets to shoot.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    </ol>

